      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ayr%2C_North_Dakota"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town was officially founded in October 1883 under the name Dunlop.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ayr%2C_North_Dakota"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Settlers came from Scotland, especially Edinburgh and the town of Ayr, in the 1880s.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ayr%2C_North_Dakota"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The first shop in Ayr was built in 1884 by Dave Francis.",
